TOOL=codex
TIMEOUT=1800
CAPTURE_STDOUT=false
CAPTURE_STDOUT_ONLY=false
OUTPUT_FILE=<TMPDIR>/step2b-codex-raw.40749.txt
CMD_JSON=["codex","exec","--sandbox","read-only","-C","<OPERATOR_REPO_PATH>","--add-dir","<OPERATOR_REPO_PATH>","-m","gpt-5.5","-c","projects.\"/Users/zhupanov/larch8\".trust_level=\"trusted\"","-c","model_provider=\"openai-larch-env\"","-c","model_providers.openai-larch-env.name=\"OpenAI API (larch env key)\"","-c","model_providers.openai-larch-env.base_url=\"https://api.openai.com/v1\"","-c","model_providers.openai-larch-env.env_key=\"OPENAI_API_KEY\"","-c","model_providers.openai-larch-env.wire_api=\"responses\"","--output-last-message","<TMPDIR>/step2b-codex-raw.40749.txt","--json","--","You are an expert engineer researching this repository and producing an implementation plan for /design Step 2b.\n\nYou may use only side-effect-free repository discovery. Do not write repository files, design tmpdir files, or any other files. Return only the sentinel-delimited response requested below.\n\nDrafting requirements to follow:\n- Prefer minimum necessary change: avoid scope creep, unnecessary complexity, and additions not required for correctness.\n- Read approach-synthesis.txt: if it is exactly NO_SKETCHES, draft from direct codebase/doc inspection without fabricating planning-panel agreement.\n- Read discussion-round1.md when present for scope boundaries and strict constraints.\n- Read design-outline.md only when non-empty and .outline-approved exists; treat Goals, Non-goals, and Surfaces as binding scope.\n- Read brainstorm.md when present as additive ideation context for plan drafting.\n- Use a Files to modify/create section with per-file headings exactly one path each: ### NEW:, ### UPDATED:, or ### REWRITTEN: (at least one ASCII space after ### before the keyword).\n- Include Approach, Edge cases, Failure modes when non-trivial, Testing strategy, optional diff_added/diff_deleted/mechanical_churn trailers, and final diff_lines: <N>. mechanical_churn accepts only true or false; never write a number there.\n- The final plan body must end with a whole-line diff_lines: <N> trailer.\n- Optionally include up to three dynamic plan-review archetypes in a scout block after the plan. The launcher validates, filters, caps, and materializes this block; invalid post-plan scout output is ignored.\n- Scout sentinels inside the summary or plan are fatal format errors. Never put LARCH_SCOUT_* markers in the plan body.\n\nReadability style (trusted):\n# Readability Style\n\n**Consumer**: `/design` prompt surfaces that produce user-facing text, either through an external-agent prompt token or through inline orchestration prose.\n\n**Contract**: this file is the only source of truth for the `/design` readability preamble. External prompt files embed the literal `<READABILITY_STYLE>` token, and assembly code or orchestration expands it to this full file. Inline composition sites read this file before writing user-facing text.\n\n**When to load**: load only when a `/design` step is about to compose user-facing prose or render a prompt that asks another agent to compose such prose. Do not load during setup, pure validation, or byte-stable artifact handling.\n\n---\n\n## Style Axes\n\nWrite in three styles at once:\n\n- **Strunk & White**: use active voice. Omit needless words. Prefer concrete nouns and verbs.\n- **Dyslexia-friendly**: use short sentences. Prefer simple words. Break dense ideas into headings and bullets.\n- **Brevity**: shorter is better. Minimize the total artifact length while preserving meaning.\n- **No em dashes**: never use em dashes; use periods, commas, colons, or semicolons instead.\n- **Hedge vs. direct**: hedge uncertain claims (\"may contain\", \"can fail\") instead of absolutes; keep directives imperative.\n\n## Precision Contract\n\nKeep these byte-stable unless the task explicitly edits them:\n\n- fenced code blocks\n- backticked tokens\n- file paths\n- identifiers\n- flag names\n- `### NEW:` / `### UPDATED:` / `### REWRITTEN:` plan grammar\n- the trailing `diff_lines: <N>` line\n\nDo not rewrite those items for style. Explain around them instead.\n\n## Plan-Drafting Reminders\n\nWhen `/design` Step 2b drafts a plan that adds, removes, or converts\nBash fences in `skills/implement/SKILL.md`:\n\n- List `### UPDATED: scripts/test-implement-fence-shape.sh` in\n  **Files to modify/create**.\n- Note that `EXPECTED_OLD` / `EXPECTED_NEW` may need updates.\n\nThis is a discoverability reminder only. Do not add plan grammar.\n\n## Precedence\n\nWhen rules conflict, use this order:\n\n`code references > meaning > brevity > dyslexia-friendly chunking > Strunk & White micro-rewrites`\n\nApply it directly:\n\n- Preserve code references first.\n- Preserve exact meaning next.\n- Cut words before adding layout.\n- Add headings or bullets only when they improve scanning.\n- Polish grammar last.\n\n## Substitution Token\n\nExternal-agent prompt files MUST embed this literal token:\n\n`<READABILITY_STYLE>`\n\nBefore launch, replace every literal `<READABILITY_STYLE>` token with the full contents of this file.\n\n## Examples\n\nBefore: \"It is recommended that the implementer should consider adding a validation step.\"\n\nAfter: \"Add a validation step.\"\n\nBefore: \"The plan should make sure that users are not able to continue when the file cannot be read.\"\n\nAfter: \"Block the flow when the file cannot be read.\"\n\nBefore: \"In order to avoid potential future confusion, documentation can be updated.\"\n\nAfter: \"Update the docs to avoid confusion.\"\n\nBefore: \"The script performs an operation that checks if the path exists.\"\n\nAfter: \"The script checks that the path exists.\"\n\nBefore: \"This could possibly be out of scope depending on how the team wants to proceed.\"\n\nAfter: \"This may be out of scope.\"\n\nRequired output format:\n[optional]\nLARCH_SUMMARY_BEGIN\nA concise summary for large-plan preview. Omit this whole summary block only when no useful summary is needed.\nLARCH_SUMMARY_END\n[/optional]\nLARCH_PLAN_BEGIN\nFull implementation plan body ending with diff_lines: <N>.\nLARCH_PLAN_END\n[optional]\nLARCH_SCOUT_BEGIN\n{\"archetypes\":[{\"name\":\"slug\",\"focus_area\":\"code-quality|risk-integration|correctness|architecture|security\",\"weight\":1,\"rationale\":\"single-line reason\",\"prompt_body\":\"2-6 sentence focus directive ending with the required citation sentence.\"}]}\nLARCH_SCOUT_END\n[/optional]\n\nOptional advisory status may be included between LARCH_STATUS_BEGIN and LARCH_STATUS_END, but the summary, plan, and optional scout sentinels above are the only parsed contract.\n\nUntrusted feature description:\n<feature_description encoding=\"literal-redacted\">\n# [BUG] (URGENT) Vendor agents health check overhaul (Step 0 in particular)\n\n1. There should be retries in the health check -- verify\n2. If, after retries, one or both of {Cursor, Codex} vendors are determined to be unhealthy, the user should get a big warning and asked to confirm before moving forward.  If BOTH of them are down, the skill should hard fail and refuse to proceed.\n3. All places that call vendors should NOT be relying on global health info -- Step 0 health check purpose should be reduced to insuring (2) warning/confirmation happens, not providing useful info for calling sites.  The clients invoking these agents (e.g., review process) have their own ways of invoking them with retries, and we should let those retries take care of short glitches in availability.\n4. The concept of \"global variable\" of agent health state should be eliminated.\n5. The caller sites should NOT retry if binary is missing or is not executable, they should only retry if it runs but fails with non-0 exit code.\n\n&lt;!-- larch:plan:start --&gt;\n## Plan\n\n## Approach\n\n- Keep the existing probe retry counts.\n- Treat Step 0 health as a user-safety gate only.\n- Stop writing `/design` health-state globals into durable env.\n- Stop using probe health to decide which vendor slots, coders, reviewers, fixers, scouts, or revisers to launch.\n- Use binary presence only for choices where an impossible command should be skipped before launch.\n- For reviewer and voter manifests that should expose missing external reviewers as degradation, keep the external slots attempted and let launcher fast-fail missing binaries.\n- Retry only when a vendor binary exists and the vendor command exits non-zero.\n- Do not retry launcher attempts when the pre-spawn health gate already fast-failed for a missing or non-executable binary.\n- Make one-vendor-down a blocking operator decision unless an explicit continue sentinel already exists.\n- Make both-vendors-down a hard fail in every mode, including CI, non-interactive, and re-entry with a stale sentinel.\n\n## Files to modify/create\n\n### UPDATED: python/agents.py\n\n- Remove `CODEX_AVAILABLE` and `CURSOR_AVAILABLE` from `CheckReviewersResult.kv()` and `kv_lines()`.\n- Keep `CODEX_PRESENT` and `CURSOR_PRESENT` as immediate probe output for Step 0 degraded-tools gates.\n- Update `degraded_tools_result()` text:\n  - one vendor down: explain that Step 0 requires explicit operator confirmation.\n  - both vendors down: explain that the run cannot continue.\n  - remove stale wording that says `/design` omits manifest slots based on global availability.\n  - say later vendor callers run their own launch, retry, and fallback logic.\n- Update `degraded_tools_gate_main()` to emit a terminal marker for both-down, for example `DEGRADED_HARD_FAIL=true`, while preserving `DEGRADED`, `BOTH_DOWN`, and state KVs.\n- In Python `_external_health_gate()`, check `shutil.which(tool)` before the retry loop.\n  - If the binary is absent or not executable, return unhealthy immediately.\n  - Include a diagnostic such as `health-probe fast-fail: codex binary missing or not executable`.\n  - Do not sleep or call `check_reviewers()` on this path.\n  - Keep existing retry behavior for non-zero probe results when the binary exists.\n- In `_review_run_with_retries()` or `is_transient_infra_failure()`, do not treat health-gate fast-fail diagnostics as retryable transient failures.\n- Update tests that assert reviewer KV order.\n- Add tests for:\n  - one-down degraded result requires a prompt path.\n  - both-down emits the hard-fail marker.\n  - Python health gate does not retry when the binary is missing.\n  - Python health gate still retries transient non-zero probe failures when the binary exists.\n  - missing-binary health-gate fast-fail performs one outer launch attempt only.\n\n### UPDATED: python/session_env.py\n\n- In `write_design_env_main()`, stop writing `CODEX_PRESENT`, `CURSOR_PRESENT`, `CODEX_AVAILABLE`, and `CURSOR_AVAILABLE` to `/design` source env files.\n- Keep accepting the legacy CLI flags for compatibility.\n- Validate legacy health flags when supplied, then discard them instead of persisting them.\n- Keep writing `CODEX_BINARY_FOUND` and `CURSOR_BINARY_FOUND`.\n- Remove recovery of prior `*_PRESENT` and `*_AVAILABLE` values for design env output.\n- Keep `session setup --check-reviewers` probe output unchanged enough for Step 0 to consume explicit probe KVs before env writing.\n\n### UPDATED: skills/design/scripts/design-step0-session.sh\n\n- Parse `CODEX_PRESENT` and `CURSOR_PRESENT` from `session setup` stdout only for the immediate degraded-tools gate.\n- Stop passing `--codex-present`, `--cursor-present`, `--codex-available`, and `--cursor-available` into `session write-design-env`.\n- Continue passing `--codex-binary-found` and `--cursor-binary-found`.\n- Change degraded gate branching:\n  - healthy: `STEP0_STATUS=ok`.\n  - one vendor down with no prior explicit continue sentinel: `STEP0_STATUS=needs-degraded-decision` and `DEGRADED_PROMPT_REQUIRED=true`.\n  - one vendor down with the sentinel already written: `STEP0_STATUS=degraded-one-down`.\n  - both vendors down in any mode: `STEP0_STATUS=degraded-both-down-hard-fail` and `DEGRADED_HARD_FAIL=true`.\n- Remove the `degraded-both-down-auto` path.\n- Do not write `.degraded-tools-gate-prompted` from the one-down detection path.\n- Write or honor the sentinel only after an explicit operator Continue decision.\n- Remove non-interactive auto-proceed for one-down unless there is already an explicit continue sentinel from a prior operator decision.\n- Ignore any sentinel when both vendors are down.\n\n### UPDATED: skills/shared/external-reviewers.md\n\n- Update the canonical Step 0 degraded-tools gate procedure.\n- Define the shared contract:\n  - healthy proceeds.\n  - one vendor down without a sentinel requires explicit operator confirmation.\n  - one vendor down with a sentinel may proceed degraded.\n  - both vendors down hard-fails in all modes.\n- Remove one-down auto-proceed language.\n- Remove both-down Continue/Abort language.\n- Remove non-interactive degraded auto-proceed language.\n- For non-interactive, CI, eval, and subagent contexts, emit a prompt-required or terminal envelope instead of proceeding without confirmation.\n- State that Step 0 probe health is not a routing input for later vendor calls.\n- State that later callers must use binary presence or launcher-owned retry and fallback behavior.\n- Keep sentinel semantics explicit: only a prior operator Continue can create the continue sentinel.\n\n### UPDATED: skills/design/SKILL.md\n\n- In Step 0a, stop instructing the orchestrator to parse or bind `codex_available` / `cursor_available` mental booleans.\n- Update Step 0 status handling:\n  - `ok` and resumed `degraded-one-down` proceed.\n  - `needs-degraded-decision` fires a blocking `AskUserQuestion` with Continue or Abort.\n  - `degraded-both-down-hard-fail` stops the skill in all modes.\n  - remove `degraded-both-down-auto`.\n- Update the AskUserQuestion copy to make the warning prominent.\n- Remove \"The gate does not flip `codex_available` / `cursor_available`.\"\n- Remove the Step 3 \"External Reviewer Setup (if `codex_available` or `cursor_available`)\" condition.\n- Keep the Step 3 requirement that all static and eligible dynamic reviewers launch, with per-slot fallback handled by the review driver.\n- Update brainstorm launch prose so external brainstorm calls are not skipped based on Step 0 probe health.\n- Use `CODEX_BINARY_FOUND` / `CURSOR_BINARY_FOUND` or launcher fast-fail semantics for any remaining prompt-side vendor launch decisions.\n\n### UPDATED: skills/implement/SKILL.md\n\n- Update the absorbed continue tail description to match the new shared degraded-tools procedure.\n- State that `_run_absorbed_continue_tail()` stops before checkpoint `1.r` when both vendors are down.\n- State that one vendor down without a sentinel emits `DEGRADED_PROMPT_REQUIRED=true` and does not auto-continue.\n- Remove non-interactive auto-proceed degraded language.\n- Document that a stale `.degraded-tools-gate-prompted` sentinel never permits both-down continuation.\n- Update Step 0 routing prose so `/implement` treats probe health as a warning or hard-fail gate only.\n\n### UPDATED: skills/review/SKILL.md\n\n- Replace the local Step 0 degraded branch prose with the shared contract.\n- Remove interactive one-down notice-only proceed.\n- Remove both-down Continue/Abort proceed.\n- Remove subagent and non-interactive degraded auto-proceed.\n- State that `/review --subagent` cannot ask the user, so it must stop with a prompt-required envelope on one-down without a sentinel.\n- Keep review panel dispatch independent of Step 0 probe health.\n\n### UPDATED: skills/research/SKILL.md\n\n- Replace the local Step 0 degraded branch prose with the shared contract.\n- Remove one-down auto-proceed.\n- Remove both-down Continue/Abort proceed.\n- Remove non-interactive degraded auto-proceed.\n- Keep research lane topology independent of Step 0 probe health.\n- State that Codex/Cursor lane launches use binary presence or launcher fallback, not persisted health globals.\n\n### UPDATED: python/bootstrap.py\n\n- Stop deriving `st.codex_available` / `st.cursor_available` from `CODEX_PRESENT` / `CURSOR_PRESENT`.\n- Derive coder availability from `CODEX_BINARY_FOUND` / `CURSOR_BINARY_FOUND` only.\n- Keep the existing coder preference order.\n- Keep explicit `--coder codex` / `--coder cursor` behavior, but mark unavailable only when the requested binary is missing.\n- Leave Step 0 degraded-tools gate use of probe presence intact for warning and hard-fail only.\n- Update routing/env output if it currently exposes `codex_available` / `cursor_available`, making those values binary-derived or removing them from routing decisions.\n- Rework `_run_absorbed_continue_tail()`:\n  - parse `DEGRADED_HARD_FAIL=true` and `BOTH_DOWN=true`.\n  - return a terminal failure before `1.r` for both-down in all modes.\n  - ignore any existing degraded sentinel when both-down is true.\n  - emit `DEGRADED_PROMPT_REQUIRED=true` for one-down when no sentinel exists.\n  - do not auto-write `.degraded-tools-gate-prompted`.\n  - proceed on one-down only when the explicit continue sentinel already exists.\n- Update `/implement` routing text and envelopes so the user sees a clear degraded-gate reason instead of a generic bootstrap failure.\n\n### UPDATED: python/implement_dispatch.py\n\n- Stop using `CURSOR_PRESENT` to refuse or fall back from a selected Cursor coder.\n- Gate Cursor dispatch on `CURSOR_BINARY_FOUND=true` or a fresh executable check.\n- Apply the same binary-only rule to any Codex dispatch guard if present.\n- Keep legacy `CURSOR_PRESENT` / `CODEX_PRESENT` values accepted when read from older env files, but do not use them as health gates.\n- Preserve explicit coder selection semantics.\n- Let launcher retry and fallback handle runtime vendor failures after binary presence is confirmed.\n\n### UPDATED: python/review_and_fix.py\n\n- Stop using `CODEX_PRESENT` and `CURSOR_PRESENT` as Step 5 coder/fixer skip gates.\n- In `_run_coder_codex()` and `_run_coder_cursor()`, remove probe-health env checks.\n- Keep binary and auth preflight checks.\n- Derive fix-application tier availability from `CODEX_BINARY_FOUND` / `CURSOR_BINARY_FOUND` or `shutil.which()`.\n- Keep legacy CLI args and session values accepted for compatibility, but do not map probe-health false to unavailable.\n- Avoid exporting probe-health-derived `CODEX_PRESENT` / `CURSOR_PRESENT` to downstream fix paths.\n- Add a regression where probe health is false but the binary exists and the fixer still attempts that vendor.\n\n### UPDATED: python/legacy_review_shell/review-core.sh\n\n- Stop using `CODEX_AVAILABLE` and `CURSOR_AVAILABLE` as Step 0 health gates for review routing.\n- Keep deprecated args accepted and validated when supplied.\n- Convert any external reviewer or voter routing to binary-derived attempt flags or unconditional attempted slots, depending on the existing review contract for that phase.\n- Pass attempt flags to downstream waterfall dispatch that do not come from Step 0 probe health.\n- Keep failed external launches visible as degraded reviewer results instead of silently reducing the panel.\n\n### UPDATED: python/legacy_review_shell/dispatch-panel.sh\n\n- Stop building panel slots from `CODEX_AVAILABLE` / `CURSOR_AVAILABLE` Step 0 health.\n- Use binary presence or unconditional external-slot launch.\n- Pass `--codex-present true` / `--cursor-present true` where the manifest should attempt the external reviewer and rely on launcher fast-fail.\n- Remove skip branches that suppress Codex or Cursor solely because Step 0 probe health was false.\n- Keep no-fallback and fallback behavior otherwise unchanged.\n\n### UPDATED: python/legacy_review_shell/tally-code-votes.sh\n\n- Stop lowering expected code-vote counts based on `CODEX_AVAILABLE` / `CURSOR_AVAILABLE`.\n- Keep deprecated args accepted for compatibility.\n- Count configured external voters consistently with the dispatch manifest.\n- Let actual missing binaries or launch failures appear as failed or missing external votes.\n\n### UPDATED: scripts/dispatch-code-voters.sh\n\n- Stop using `CODEX_AVAILABLE` and `CURSOR_AVAILABLE` to skip voter slots.\n- Keep `--codex-available` and `--cursor-available` as accepted deprecated args for compatibility, or make them optional if all callers are updated in the same change.\n- Pass `--codex-present true` and `--cursor-present true` to `dispatch-with-waterfall.sh` so both external slots are attempted.\n- Keep `--no-fallback` so failed external voter slots are dropped instead of backfilled by duplicate judges.\n- Remove `VOTER_2_STATUS=skipped` / `VOTER_3_STATUS=skipped` based on Step 0 availability.\n- Set `expected_judges=3` for Claude, Codex, and Cursor.\n- Let binary-missing or launcher failure become a failed external slot.\n\n### UPDATED: scripts/dispatch-with-waterfall.sh\n\n- Clarify that `--codex-present` and `--cursor-present` are per-call attempt flags, not Step 0 probe health.\n- Keep accepting `--codex-available` and `--cursor-available` aliases for compatibility.\n- Do not read global `CODEX_PRESENT`, `CURSOR_PRESENT`, `CODEX_AVAILABLE`, or `CURSOR_AVAILABLE` from the environment for routing.\n- Preserve existing no-fallback, fallback, timeout, and result-pattern behavior.\n\n### UPDATED: scripts/lib-external-launcher-common.sh\n\n- In `external_launch_health_gate()`, check the real executable path before entering the retry loop.\n- Prefer a path check that rejects shell functions and aliases where practical.\n- If the binary is missing or not executable:\n  - set the optional diagnostic var when provided.\n  - include a `health-probe fast-fail` marker.\n  - return unhealthy immediately.\n  - do not call `agent check-reviewers`.\n  - do not sleep.\n- Keep the existing retry count and sleep behavior for executable binaries that return probe failures.\n- Keep timeout opt-out behavior unchanged.\n\n### UPDATED: skills/design/scripts/design-step2b-drafter.sh\n\n- Stop preferring Codex from `CODEX_PRESENT`.\n- Prefer Codex when `CODEX_BINARY_FOUND=true` or a fresh executable check succeeds.\n- Keep `LARCH_DESIGN_DRAFTER=codex|claude` override behavior.\n- For explicit `LARCH_DESIGN_DRAFTER=codex`, fail or fallback only when the Codex binary is missing or the launcher fails.\n- Add status output that makes stale probe-health false irrelevant to drafter vendor choice.\n\n### UPDATED: skills/design/scripts/design-step-validator-autofix.sh\n\n- Stop passing `CODEX_PRESENT`, `CURSOR_PRESENT`, `CODEX_AVAILABLE`, and `CURSOR_AVAILABLE` into plan autofix as routing inputs.\n- Pass binary-found flags if the CLI keeps explicit binary args, or omit legacy health args once they are optional.\n- Keep validation, tmpdir, and repo guard behavior unchanged.\n\n### UPDATED: skills/design/scripts/review-design-step3-loop.sh\n\n- Stop passing `CODEX_PRESENT` and `CURSOR_PRESENT` from sourced design env into `plan revise-waterfall`.\n- Pass binary-derived attempt flags or omit legacy flags after the Python CLI makes them optional.\n- Preserve round phase transitions and failure codes.\n- Add a regression where Step 0 probe health is false but binary-found is true and revise-waterfall still attempts the external tier.\n\n### UPDATED: python/plan_quality.py\n\n- In `auto_fix_plan_commands_main()`, stop building the vendor sequence from `--codex-present`, `--cursor-present`, `--codex-available`, or `--cursor-available`.\n- Keep those arguments accepted for CLI compatibility if removing them would break callers.\n- Build the vendor list from executable binary presence, for example `shutil.which(\"codex\")` and `shutil.which(\"cursor\")`.\n- If no vendor binary exists for autofix, emit the current unavailable envelope and do not attempt fixes.\n- If a binary exists, attempt that vendor and rely on the launcher's own retry/failure handling.\n- In `revise_plan_with_waterfall_main()`, stop skipping tiers based on `--codex-present` or `--cursor-present`.\n- Derive revise tiers from binary presence or explicit per-call binary-found args.\n- Preserve Claude fallback when no external binary is available or all external attempts fail.\n- Keep max-attempt clamping, plan validation, patch-format handling, and tmpdir/repo guard behavior unchanged.\n\n### UPDATED: python/plan_review.py\n\n- Update embedded `dispatch-plan-review-panel.sh` behavior so plan-review panel slots are not gated on Step 0 probe health.\n- Update embedded `dispatch-plan-voters.sh` behavior so voter slots are not suppressed by stale `CODEX_PRESENT` / `CURSOR_PRESENT` false values.\n- Use binary-derived attempt flags or unconditional external slot attempts with launcher fast-fail.\n- Keep static reviewer slots and eligible dynamic reviewer slots launched.\n- Preserve no-fallback behavior where duplicate judges must not backfill failed external voters.\n- Update embedded asset bytes and any sync or retirement checks that validate those assets.\n\n### UPDATED: python/plan_scout.py\n\n- Stop using `cursor_present` from Step 0 probe health to decide whether to attempt the Cursor scout tier.\n- Keep `codex_present` and `cursor_present` args accepted for caller parity.\n- Derive scout tier attempts from binary presence or explicit binary-found args.\n- Keep Cursor-to-Claude fallback ordering.\n- Add a regression where `--cursor-present false` with a Cursor executable still attempts Cursor before Claude.\n\n### UPDATED: python/decompose.py\n\n- Stop using `codex_present` and `cursor_present` probe-health args to decide decompose panel and aggregate vendor slots.\n- Keep legacy args accepted and validated.\n- Derive decompose external slots from binary presence or unconditional per-manifest attempt semantics.\n- Preserve Claude fallback and existing result-pattern requirements.\n- Add regressions for probe false plus binary true on panel dispatch and aggregate.\n\n### UPDATED: python/run_context.py\n\n- Stop treating `CODEX_PRESENT` and `CURSOR_PRESENT` from source env files as durable routing facts.\n- Preserve compatibility for old run summaries only as nullable historical metadata.\n- Prefer `CODEX_BINARY_FOUND` and `CURSOR_BINARY_FOUND` for any current availability labels.\n\n### UPDATED: python/test_agents.py\n\n- Update `check_reviewers` KV expectations after removing `CODEX_AVAILABLE` and `CURSOR_AVAILABLE`.\n- Add degraded-gate coverage for:\n  - one vendor down.\n  - both vendors down.\n  - explicit hard-fail marker.\n- Add Python `_external_health_gate()` binary-missing fast-fail coverage.\n- Add launch-review outer retry coverage showing health-probe fast-fail is not retried.\n\n### UPDATED: python/test_session_env.py\n\n- Update `/design` env writer expectations:\n  - `CODEX_PRESENT`, `CURSOR_PRESENT`, `CODEX_AVAILABLE`, and `CURSOR_AVAILABLE` are absent.\n  - `CODEX_BINARY_FOUND` and `CURSOR_BINARY_FOUND` remain when supplied.\n- Update strict recovery tests so prior health-state globals are not recovered.\n- Keep `session setup --check-reviewers` tests focused on setup stdout and session env output where that command still writes implement/session-level probe results.\n- Add a legacy flag compatibility test proving accepted health flags are validated and discarded for design env output.\n\n### UPDATED: python/test_bootstrap.py\n\n- Update coder-selection matrix to use binary-found inputs instead of probe-health availability.\n- Add a regression where `CODEX_PRESENT=false` and `CODEX_BINARY_FOUND=true` still allows Codex coder selection.\n- Add a regression where `CODEX_BINARY_FOUND=false` causes fallback even if stale probe health says true.\n- Update expected routing output for `codex_available` / `cursor_available` if those remain as binary-derived internal labels.\n- Add absorbed-tail coverage:\n  - both-down hard-fails in interactive mode.\n  - both-down hard-fails in non-interactive mode.\n  - both-down ignores a prior sentinel.\n  - one-down without sentinel emits `DEGRADED_PROMPT_REQUIRED=true`.\n  - one-down with sentinel proceeds to `1.r`.\n\n### UPDATED: python/test_implement_dispatch.py\n\n- Replace `CURSOR_PRESENT=false` refusal expectations with `CURSOR_BINARY_FOUND=false` or missing executable expectations.\n- Add a regression where `CURSOR_PRESENT=false` and `CURSOR_BINARY_FOUND=true` still dispatches Cursor.\n- Add stale-health true plus binary-missing coverage that still refuses or falls back.\n- Keep invalid legacy value parsing tests only where the value is still parsed for compatibility.\n\n### UPDATED: python/test_review_and_fix.py\n\n- Update coder/fixer waterfall tests so Step 0 probe-health false does not skip Codex or Cursor.\n- Add regressions for:\n  - `CODEX_PRESENT=false` with a Codex executable still attempts Codex.\n  - `CURSOR_PRESENT=false` with a Cursor executable still attempts Cursor.\n  - missing binary still skips or fails fast before launcher retry.\n- Keep auth and non-zero launcher failure tests unchanged.\n\n### UPDATED: python/test_plan_quality.py\n\n- Update auto-fix tests so vendor selection no longer depends on `--codex-present` / `--cursor-present`.\n- Add executable-presence fixtures for Codex and Cursor.\n- Add a no-binary fixture that emits `AUTOFIX_STATUS=unavailable`.\n- Add a stale-health fixture where present/available args are false but executable stubs exist, and assert auto-fix still attempts vendors.\n- Add revise-waterfall fixtures for:\n  - stale present args false plus executable stubs.\n  - no external binaries with Claude fallback preserved.\n  - external launcher failure followed by fallback.\n  - legacy args accepted but ignored for routing.\n\n### UPDATED: python/test_plan_review.py\n\n- Update embedded asset and compatibility expectations after changing plan-review dispatch behavior.\n- Add coverage that plan-review panel and voter dispatch inputs are not derived from Step 0 probe health.\n- Add stale-health false plus binary true regressions for embedded dispatch assets where practical.\n\n### UPDATED: python/test_plan_review_panel.py\n\n- Update panel expectations so Codex and Cursor slots are attempted independent of Step 0 health.\n- Keep dynamic reviewer cap and archetype filtering behavior unchanged.\n- Add a regression that failed external slots are reported rather than silently omitted due to stale health.\n\n### UPDATED: python/test_plan_scout.py\n\n- Update scout tests to use binary presence instead of `cursor_present` for launch eligibility.\n- Add stale-health false plus Cursor executable coverage.\n- Keep Cursor-to-Claude fallback behavior tests.\n\n### UPDATED: python/test_decompose.py\n\n- Update decompose panel and aggregate tests to ignore probe-health args for routing.\n- Add binary-present fixtures for Codex and Cursor.\n- Add stale-health false plus binary true coverage.\n- Keep malformed manifest and result-pattern failure tests unchanged.\n\n### UPDATED: skills/design/scripts/test-design-step2b-drafter.sh\n\n- Update fixtures from `CODEX_PRESENT` to `CODEX_BINARY_FOUND` or executable stubs.\n- Add a regression where `CODEX_PRESENT=false` but `CODEX_BINARY_FOUND=true` still selects Codex by default.\n- Add a regression where binary missing falls back to Claude.\n\n### UPDATED: skills/design/scripts/test-auto-fix-plan-commands.sh\n\n- Update auto-fix harnesses so stale Step 0 health flags do not suppress external vendors.\n- Add executable stubs for positive Codex/Cursor cases.\n- Keep no-binary unavailable behavior.\n\n### UPDATED: skills/design/scripts/test-design-step3-review.sh\n\n- Update Step 3 revise-waterfall fixtures to use binary-derived routing.\n- Add stale-health false plus binary true coverage.\n- Preserve phase transition assertions.\n\n### UPDATED: scripts/test-lib-external-launcher-common.sh\n\n- Add a health-gate case where `codex` or `cursor` is absent from `PATH`.\n- Assert:\n  - return code is unhealthy.\n  - checker-call file is not created.\n  - no retry sleep is observed when attempts are set above 1.\n  - diagnostic text mentions missing or non-executable binary.\n  - diagnostic text includes the fast-fail marker used by outer retry suppression.\n- Keep existing retry-recovery tests unchanged.\n\n### UPDATED: scripts/test-dispatch-code-voters.sh\n\n- Update fixtures that pass `--codex-available false` or `--cursor-available false`.\n- Assert the dispatcher still writes both external slots into the waterfall manifest.\n- Assert unavailable Step 0 args no longer produce `skipped` voter statuses.\n- Assert `expected_judges=3` remains stable.\n- Keep failure and timeout assertions for actual failed external launches.\n\n### UPDATED: scripts/test-design-structure.sh\n\n- Remove assertions that require `degraded-both-down-auto`.\n- Remove assertions that require both-down sentinel short-circuit proceed.\n- Add assertions for the new hard-fail marker and terminal both-down status.\n- Add assertions that first one-down emits `DEGRADED_PROMPT_REQUIRED=true`.\n- Add assertions that the one-down path does not auto-create the continue sentinel.\n\n### UPDATED: scripts/test-implement-structure.sh\n\n- Update structure assertions that require `read_session_key CODEX_PRESENT` / `CURSOR_PRESENT` for routing.\n- Add assertions for absorbed-tail both-down hard fail.\n- Add assertions for one-down prompt-required behavior.\n- Reject non-interactive degraded auto-proceed language.\n\n### UPDATED: scripts/test-review-structure.sh\n\n- Update Step 0 structure assertions to match the shared degraded-tools contract.\n- Reject one-down auto-proceed and both-down Continue/Abort proceed.\n- Ensure `/review --subagent` does not auto-proceed degraded without prior sentinel.\n\n### UPDATED: scripts/test-research-structure.sh\n\n- Update Step 0 structure assertions to match the shared degraded-tools contract.\n- Reject non-interactive degraded auto-proceed.\n- Ensure research lane topology is not described as probe-health-derived.\n\n### UPDATED: docs/external-reviewers.md\n\n- Sync user-facing degraded-tools gate documentation with `skills/shared/external-reviewers.md`.\n- State that Step 0 probe health is a warning or hard-fail gate only.\n- State that vendor callers use launcher retry, fallback, and binary fast-fail behavior rather than global health variables.\n\n## Edge cases\n\n- Re-entry after a prior one-down Continue should not re-prompt.\n- Re-entry after both-down must still stop, even if `.degraded-tools-gate-prompted` exists.\n- Non-interactive one-down without a sentinel must not auto-proceed.\n- `/review --subagent` one-down without a sentinel must stop with a prompt-required envelope because it cannot ask the operator.\n- Empty `CODEX_PRESENT` or `CURSOR_PRESENT` from Step 0 remains a caller bug signal and should fail safe as down for the Step 0 gate only.\n- Legacy callers may still pass `--codex-available`, `--cursor-available`, `--codex-present`, or `--cursor-present`; accept but ignore those values for routing where needed.\n- Binary presence is not health. A found binary can still fail and should use existing launcher retry/failure paths.\n- Missing or non-executable binaries should fast-fail before probe retries and before outer launch retries.\n- `command -v` can find shell functions in some contexts. Prefer executable path checks where practical.\n- Embedded plan-review assets and compatibility tests must be updated together.\n- Expected reviewer and voter counts must not shrink silently because Step 0 probe health was false.\n- Stale source env files from older sessions may contain health globals; do not let them override binary-derived routing.\n\n## Failure modes\n\n- If `session write-design-env` removes too much, later design fences may lose `CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT`, `DESIGN_TMPDIR`, or binary-found state.\n- If Step 0 exits non-zero without a clear terminal envelope, the user may see a misleading generic session setup failure.\n- If one-down non-interactive runs still auto-proceed, CI can mask degraded reviewer coverage.\n- If both-down re-entry honors a stale sentinel, `/design` or `/implement` can continue when the new contract requires refusal.\n- If dispatch-code-voters keeps expected judges at 2 or 1, failed external launches may not be reported as degradation.\n- If auto-fix or revise-waterfall treats missing binaries as retryable failures, it can waste attempts and time.\n- If outer launch retry treats health-probe fast-fail as transient, missing binaries can still burn multiple launch attempts.\n- If `CheckReviewersResult.kv_lines()` order changes unexpectedly, shell parsers and tests may fail.\n- If embedded plan-review assets are not regenerated or updated, compatibility tests may pass old routing into runtime.\n- If review-and-fix exports stale `CODEX_PRESENT=false` / `CURSOR_PRESENT=false`, downstream legacy shell can still skip external fix tiers.\n- If docs and shared skill prose diverge, `/review` or `/research` can preserve the old degraded UX.\n\n## Testing strategy\n\n- Run focused Python tests:\n  - `python3 -m pytest python/test_agents.py python/test_session_env.py python/test_bootstrap.py python/test_implement_dispatch.py python/test_review_and_fix.py`\n  - `python3 -m pytest python/test_plan_quality.py python/test_plan_review.py python/test_plan_review_panel.py python/test_plan_scout.py python/test_decompose.py`\n- Run focused shell harnesses:\n  - `scripts/test-lib-external-launcher-common.sh`\n  - `scripts/test-dispatch-code-voters.sh`\n  - `scripts/test-design-structure.sh`\n  - `scripts/test-implement-structure.sh`\n  - `scripts/test-review-structure.sh`\n  - `scripts/test-research-structure.sh`\n  - `skills/design/scripts/test-design-step2b-drafter.sh`\n  - `skills/design/scripts/test-auto-fix-plan-commands.sh`\n  - `skills/design/scripts/test-design-step3-review.sh`\n- Run broader required checks:\n  - `make py-lint`\n  - `make py-test`\n  - `make lint`\n- Manually inspect Step 0 wrapper output for:\n  - both healthy.\n  - Codex down only.\n  - Cursor down only.\n  - both down.\n  - one-down re-entry after sentinel.\n  - both-down re-entry with stale sentinel.\n  - non-interactive one-down.\n- Verify no `/design` source env contains `CODEX_PRESENT`, `CURSOR_PRESENT`, `CODEX_AVAILABLE`, or `CURSOR_AVAILABLE`.\n- Verify `/design` source env still contains `CODEX_BINARY_FOUND` and `CURSOR_BINARY_FOUND` when known.\n- Verify vendor caller regressions where probe health is false but binary-found is true:\n  - Step 2b drafter.\n  - brainstorm.\n  - Step 3 panel.\n  - Step 3 voters.\n  - revise-waterfall.\n  - scout.\n  - decompose.\n  - implement dispatch.\n  - review-and-fix.\n  - code-review panel.\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- Round 1 plan review passed with 9 accepted findings (all applied).\n- Plan reviewed by 14 slots (8 static + 6 dynamic) across Cursor and Codex.\n- Session terminated by operator before Round 2 completed; plan reflects Round 1 findings only.\n\ndiff_lines: 990\n&lt;!-- larch:plan:end --&gt;\n\n\n</feature_description>\n\n\nUntrusted approach synthesis:\n<approach_synthesis encoding=\"literal-redacted\">\nNO_SKETCHES\n\n</approach_synthesis>\n\n\nUntrusted discussion round 1:\n<discussion_round1 encoding=\"literal-redacted\">\n## Decision 1: Probe retry counts are preserved\n- **Question**: Do the existing retry counts in `check_reviewers()` satisfy the issue's \"there should be retries\" requirement?\n- **Resolution**: Yes. `check_reviewers()` already retries via `_run_codex_probes`/`_run_cursor_probes` with `LARCH_EXTERNAL_AUTH_RETRIES` (default 5 for auth errors) and `LARCH_PROBE_TIMEOUT_SECONDS` (default 30). Binary-missing already short-circuits on the first attempt (no retry) because `shutil.which()` returns `None` before any probe runs.\n- **Source**: codebase\n\n## Decision 2: Both-down → true hard fail (no option to continue)\n- **Question**: When both Codex and Cursor probe-fail after retries, should Step 0 hard-fail with no AskUserQuestion?\n- **Resolution**: Yes. Print the error/explanation and exit non-zero immediately. No prompt, no option to continue. The user must fix the tooling before re-running. This changes the current `needs-degraded-decision` path for both-down.\n- **Source**: user\n\n## Decision 3: One-down → big warning + confirm (keep existing gate)\n- **Question**: When only one vendor fails, keep the existing \"warn + confirm\" AskUserQuestion gate?\n- **Resolution**: Yes. Print the degraded-tool explanation block and fire AskUserQuestion with Continue/Abort. No change to one-down behavior except the messaging should be prominent (\"big warning\").\n- **Source**: user + issue text\n\n## Decision 4: Global health state fully removed from session-env\n- **Question**: Remove CODEX_AVAILABLE/CURSOR_AVAILABLE and also CODEX_PRESENT/CURSOR_PRESENT from session-env (WRITE_ENV_KEYS, WRITE_DESIGN_ENV_KEYS)?\n- **Resolution**: Yes. Remove all four from `WRITE_ENV_KEYS` and `WRITE_DESIGN_ENV_KEYS` in session_env.py. Keep only CODEX_BINARY_FOUND/CURSOR_BINARY_FOUND (binary-on-PATH state). Callers that gated on CODEX_AVAILABLE or CODEX_PRESENT now gate on CODEX_BINARY_FOUND.\n- **Source**: user (full removal everywhere)\n\n## Decision 5: _external_health_gate removed entirely\n- **Question**: Remove `_external_health_gate` from `agents.py` and its call in `run_external_agent`?\n- **Resolution**: Yes. Remove the function and the call site. The pre-launch per-call health gate is eliminated. Calling sites rely on the waterfall/retry on failure.\n- **Source**: user\n\n## Decision 6: All caller sites switch to binary-found\n- **Question**: What replaces CODEX_AVAILABLE/CURSOR_PRESENT at calling sites (dispatch-panel.sh, dispatch-code-voters.sh, dispatch-with-waterfall.sh, bootstrap.py, review_and_fix.py, oos_filer.py)?\n- **Resolution**: Replace with CODEX_BINARY_FOUND/CURSOR_BINARY_FOUND. If binary is on PATH, attempt the slot; let the waterfall handle failures. If binary is not on PATH, skip the slot.\n- **Source**: user + codebase (dispatch-with-waterfall.sh already has the --codex-present/--cursor-present flags that callers will now pass binary-found values to)\n\n## Decision 7: scope — non-goals\n- **Question**: What is explicitly out of scope?\n- **Resolution**: We do NOT change the waterfall retry behavior (already handles failures). We do NOT change the probe command itself (same probe logic, just results are no longer written as durable globals). We do NOT add new retry mechanisms at caller sites.\n- **Source**: issue text\n\n</discussion_round1>\n\n\nUntrusted approved design outline:\n<design_outline encoding=\"literal-redacted\">\n## Proposed Design Outline\n\n### Goals\n- Reduce Step 0 health check to a user-safety gate only: warn + confirm when one vendor is down; hard-fail when both are down.\n- Remove probe-based health globals (`CODEX_AVAILABLE`, `CURSOR_AVAILABLE`, `CODEX_PRESENT`, `CURSOR_PRESENT`) from session-env and all caller decisions.\n- Eliminate the per-launch `_external_health_gate` pre-call check; callers rely on binary presence and the existing waterfall.\n\n### Non-goals\n- Do not change probe retry counts or probe command logic.\n- Do not change waterfall/fallback behavior at dispatch sites.\n- Do not add new retry mechanisms at caller sites.\n\n### Approach sketch\n- `agents.py`: Remove `_external_health_gate` + its call in `run_external_agent`; stop emitting `CODEX_AVAILABLE`/`CURSOR_AVAILABLE` from `CheckReviewersResult.kv()`; update `degraded_tools_gate_main` to emit a hard-fail signal when both are down (no prompt path).\n- `session_env.py`: Remove `CODEX_AVAILABLE`, `CURSOR_AVAILABLE`, `CODEX_PRESENT`, `CURSOR_PRESENT` from `WRITE_ENV_KEYS` and `WRITE_DESIGN_ENV_KEYS`; keep `CODEX_BINARY_FOUND`/`CURSOR_BINARY_FOUND`.\n- `bootstrap.py`: Replace `codex_available`/`cursor_available` with `codex_binary_found`/`cursor_binary_found` throughout coder-selection and emit paths.\n- Shell dispatchers (`dispatch-panel.sh`, `dispatch-code-voters.sh`, `dispatch-with-waterfall.sh`): Pass `CODEX_BINARY_FOUND`/`CURSOR_BINARY_FOUND` values instead of `CODEX_AVAILABLE`/`CURSOR_PRESENT` to waterfall flags.\n- `review_and_fix.py`, `oos_filer.py`: Switch availability checks to binary-found env vars.\n- `skills/design/SKILL.md`: Update degraded-tools-gate description for both-down hard-fail (no AskUserQuestion).\n- Tests: Update `test_agents.py`, `test_session_env.py`, `test_bootstrap.py`, `test_review_and_fix.py`, `test_oos_filer.py` to remove health-gate tests and probe-global assertions.\n\n### Surfaces in scope\n- `python/agents.py`, `python/session_env.py`, `python/bootstrap.py`\n- `python/review_and_fix.py`, `python/oos_filer.py`, `python/implement_dispatch.py`\n- `scripts/dispatch-with-waterfall.sh`, `scripts/dispatch-code-voters.sh`\n- `python/legacy_review_shell/dispatch-panel.sh`\n- `python/test_agents.py`, `python/test_session_env.py`, `python/test_bootstrap.py`\n- `python/test_review_and_fix.py`, `python/test_oos_filer.py`\n- `skills/design/SKILL.md` (both-down gate description)\n\n### Open questions\n- Does the `/implement` bootstrap hard-fail path (design-step0-session.sh) also need updating for both-down → no-prompt? (Likely yes — the session wrapper reads `BOTH_DOWN` and `STEP0_STATUS`.)\n\n</design_outline>\n\n"]
